{
 "about": "The twelve sources of the picture 'any coil', in reading order (left to right, back row first). load is the call that reads the source from the files listed (their names as downloaded). For a surface: bn_solver is the solver's largest |B.n|/|B| on a grid it never solved on. bn_check is the independent evaluator's estimate of the largest value over the whole surface and bn_check_sampled its largest at check_points random points, measured on x86-64 on the source that load returns. flux_err is the relative error of the enclosed flux on six sections. traced_lines is the largest distance of two independently traced field lines from the surface over 40 field periods, relative to its minor radius. For a source without a surface: the verdict and the arguments it rests on (torux.nonstell).",
